cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Conditional EGFR binder design: a pH-selective de novo binder pipeline
  with negative controls
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Juan David
    family-names: Hoyos Trejos
    email: juan.hoyos9@u.icesi.edu.co
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Basic Medical Sciences, Universidad Icesi, Cali,
      Colombia
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3185-2992'
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline for designing de novo protein binders that
  engage domain III of the human EGFR ectodomain preferentially at the
  acidic pH of the tumour microenvironment. Histidine networks are placed
  on BindCraft-generated interfaces under a geometric rule derived from
  measured rotamer reach, tested against a null distribution drawn from
  the same constrained pool of positions, and revalidated structurally
  against unmodified parents. Prepared for Challenge 01 of the Anthropic
  and Adaptyv 2026 protein design competition.
keywords:
  - protein design
  - de novo binder
  - EGFR
  - pH-selective binding
  - Wyman linkage
  - AlphaFold2
  - BindCraft
  - negative control
